From 7086c7c0da4428614643ea340d7be7e74ee1c57c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:05:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Rules engine, Policy Routing and guest isolation load their
 rules in one step (102.8 line)

- The rules engine queues its iptables lines and loads each table with one iptables-restore
  --noflush, and its literal objects with one ipset restore. A refused load re-runs the
  rule-by-rule path with its failure count; a refused set restore replays entry by entry and names
  the rejected entry.
- Policy Routing loads its staging chain with one restore per family before the jump moves.
- Guest isolation replaces each family's filter chains in one commit, with no part-filled window;
  the flow purge runs only when the rules, the live chains or the jumps differ from the last
  complete load.
- A domain list's saved addresses are replayed only into an empty set, so a firewall restart no
  longer gives every saved address a fresh hour. The resolver's comparison copy is built in /tmp;
  /jffs is written only on a change.
- The settings these scripts and the self-monitor read are fetched in one batch (new
  rc/reaper_nv.h helper); a failed batch falls back to single reads.
- The rules-engine revert script takes its arm marker first, rebuilds under the shared lock and is
  mode 0700.
- New rc/reaper_cc.h: the commit-confirm window and the deadline watcher, one copy for both
  engines.
- The firewall log settings file is written atomically.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
